      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Alexander Dove, a Scottish sea captain, bought a 13‑room homestead in the 1880s and became the first chair of the Footscray council.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Footscray",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "West Footscray’s railway station was rebuilt 200 metres west and opened in 2013 as part of the Regional Rail Link.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
